## Architecture: Two-Stage Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["CSV Upload"] --> B["Feature Extraction<br/>(66 features)"]
    B --> C["Scaler Transform"]
    C --> D["Stage 1: Binary Ensemble<br/>RF + XGB + MLP<br/>(Soft Voting)"]
    D -->|BENIGN| E["Return BENIGN<br/>attack_type: null"]
    D -->|ATTACK| F["Stage 2: XGBoost<br/>Multi-class<br/>(15 classes)"]
    F --> G["Return ATTACK<br/>attack_type: DDoS/Bot/etc."]
```

**Why two stages?**
- Stage 1 is fast — quickly filters benign traffic (majority)
- Stage 2 only runs on attack rows — efficient for real-world scenarios where most traffic is benign
- Binary ensemble has very high accuracy (99.6%), reducing false positives before classification

